# FIRE Calculator India — Cursor Rules

Read SPEC.md for full architecture. These rules take precedence.

## Stack
- SwiftUI + Foundation only. Zero external packages.
- iOS 16+. No UIKit unless absolutely unavoidable.
- PBXFileSystemSynchronizedRootGroup — new .swift files in `Fire Calculator India/` folder are auto-compiled.

## Architecture
- All models, calculator, colors, formatting → `FIREModels.swift` only.
- `FIREInputs` is the single source of truth, passed as `@Binding`.
- `FIRECalculator.calculate()` is a pure static function — keep it that way.
- Navigation: `NavigationStack` + `AppRoute` enum in `ContentView.swift`.
- `InvestmentMode` / `FIRETarget` → local `@State` on `InvestmentScreen` only, never in `FIREInputs`.

## Design — Non-Negotiable
- Colors: always use `.fireIndigo`, `.fireEmerald`, `.fireAmber`, `.fireSky`, `.fireRose`, `.firePurple`. Never raw hex in views.
- Backgrounds: `Color(.systemGroupedBackground)` / `Color(.secondarySystemGroupedBackground)`. Never hardcoded white/black.
- Every screen gets the indigo→purple navbar gradient (see SPEC.md §6.2).
- Cards: `.padding(16)` + `.background(Color(.secondarySystemGroupedBackground))` + `.cornerRadius(14)`.
- Primary CTA: sticky bottom, `Color.fireIndigo` fill, `.cornerRadius(14)`, `.padding(.vertical, 17)`.
- Sliders: always `.tint(.fireIndigo)`.

## Code Rules
- `onChange` → always `{ _, newValue in }` (two-parameter, iOS 17+).
- No force unwraps.
- No comments on obvious code — only comment WHY.
- `// MARK: - SectionName` in every file.
- Currency display: `.inrCompact` for hero values, `.inrFull` for sub-labels.

## Do Not
- Add Swift packages or CocoaPods.
- Add networking, analytics, or any remote calls.
- Add persistence (UserDefaults, CoreData) unless explicitly asked.
- Change FIRE multipliers (×20/×25/×33) or inflation default (6%) without updating SPEC.md.
- Use the Charts framework — the donut chart uses Canvas intentionally.
